<div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the driver&#39;s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The step &quot;Terms and first invoice&quot; opens for each car, filled in with the owner&#39;s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, <b class="gd-ui">Use these terms for every car</b> copies the first car&#39;s numbers to the others.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Missing something? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for something</b>, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the owner</b>. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Not a fit? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>, write the Reason the owner reads, and press <b class="gd-ui">Decline the application</b>. The owner is emailed for each car.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:67.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.9%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:49.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says &quot;Entered by staff&quot; and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Notes on the page are for staff only: <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b> keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> tab, or <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on an owner&#39;s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner&#39;s terms, or their other car&#39;s; change them for this car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and set it up</b>. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, <b class="gd-ui">Send the set-up email again</b> sends the owner the email with a fresh link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b> shows their portal. <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> helps them sign in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send invitation</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.4%;top:49.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:82.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer&#39;s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-mark-a-car-insured-insurer-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: &quot;Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured&quot;. It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the insurer&#39;s email arrives, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark insured</b>. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer&#39;s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One email for several cars? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark several insured</b> on the line &quot; cars wait for the insurer&quot;. Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same button is on the car: Overview (<b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>) and the Listing tab&#39;s checklist, item &quot;Not on the fleet insurance policy yet&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email &quot;Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy&quot;. Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners-who-paid-another-way-and-the-terms-you-agreed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed</h2><p class="gd-p">Two lines on To do keep an owner&#39;s money right without opening their page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Record the first and last month paid by &quot;: their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press <b class="gd-ui">Record what they paid</b>, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car&#39;s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. Never for a shareholder.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Enter the terms agreed with &quot;: their cars still use the standard grid. Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the terms</b>: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to change? Press <b class="gd-ui">Not needed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">These are correct</b>: the line does not come back.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-shareholder-s-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A shareholder&#39;s own car</h2><p class="gd-p">On the owner&#39;s page, each car has <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A shareholder&#39;s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-cancellation-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancellation refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: the refund for each cancellation tier.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When the renter cancels</th><th scope="col">Refund (default)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start</td><td>95%</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before the start</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before the start</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Under 24 hours, or after the start</td><td>0%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> sit under the name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Cars and terms: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> and History (see An owner&#39;s terms, car by car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender&#39;s permission of each car. <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason), <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> makes a car&#39;s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. Open a form and press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b> to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b>, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> puts a box&#39;s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under <b class="gd-ui">Every signature</b>. The step is done when every form is signed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b>: paste or upload the VINs, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car&#39;s terms, for each car whose terms are set.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Further down: <b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send a sign-in link to the owner portal</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A car&#39;s page has the same Government forms box (Owner &amp; documents).</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:410/1030"><img src="/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="410" height="1030"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:24.6%;top:4.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16.1%;top:32.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.5%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.2%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-terms-car-by-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s terms, car by car</h2><p class="gd-p">The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner&#39;s page and its Terms tab: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car&#39;s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not signed yet (or not approved yet): <b class="gd-ui">Save</b> applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings &gt; Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days&#39; written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner&#39;s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car&#39;s History.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.</p><p class="gd-p">The same editor is on the car&#39;s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner&#39;s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-pay-an-owner-a-flat-monthly-amount" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an owner a flat monthly amount</h2><p class="gd-p">Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Flat monthly payment</b>, type the <b class="gd-ui">Amount a month</b> (for example 900.00), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b> and, if it ends, the <b class="gd-ui">Last day</b>. Write the Reason (kept in the history).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">From that date the owner&#39;s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Back to revenue share: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars&#39; own unless you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge to the owner</b> beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner&#39;s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-change-a-signed-car-s-management-mode" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change a signed car&#39;s Management Mode</h2><p class="gd-p">Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change mode</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">New Management Mode</b> and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b>, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked for this</b> only when it is their own request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars&#39; signature and the owner is emailed the notice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Anything else (CarmaCars&#39; own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw it</b> if needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-paid-and-signed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Paid and signed</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Paid and signed</b> tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checklist and quick actions</b>. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press <b class="gd-ui">Record an official form signed in ink</b>, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same checklist sits at the top of each owner&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with <b class="gd-ui">Waiting to sign</b> (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on &quot; in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner&#39;s documents.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Forms C and D</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars&#39; witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/470"><img src="/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="470"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:57.6%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-the-earnings-calculator-on-list-your-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The earnings calculator on List your car</h2><p class="gd-p">People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, &quot;set in your agreement&quot;). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class&#39;s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. &quot;Just cheaper insurance&quot; shows the fleet policy&#39;s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown</b> and <b class="gd-ui">the monthly tracker fee shown</b>, in dollars a month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave either one empty and the page says &quot;Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement&quot; and shows the earnings &quot;before fees&quot;. No amount is ever made up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner&#39;s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-agreements-who-still-needs-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements: who still needs to sign</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Owners and partners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Agreements</b>. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line says <b class="gd-ui">Signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sent, not signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not sent</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing</b>. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows &quot;invite first&quot;: press Invite on the Owners list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner&#39;s Terms tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>&quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot; marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-fleet-supplier-the-fleet-lease" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: the fleet lease</h2><p class="gd-p">For a supplier&#39;s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier route</b>. To agree other numbers, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the lease terms</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier on file without the route: press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the lease terms</b> and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the <b class="gd-ui">Upkeep Table</b>: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add each car with <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on the owner&#39;s page. The <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b> step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car already on file: press <b class="gd-ui">Put on the lease</b> beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b>, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car&#39;s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier&#39;s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">An upkeep cost: <b class="gd-ui">Record an upkeep cost</b>. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-approve-a-fleet-supplier-s-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve a fleet supplier&#39;s cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b> like any other, with each car&#39;s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b> beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check <b class="gd-ui">Delivered on</b> (the lease starts that day) and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows &quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot;. The default lease terms are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Owners &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner</b> offers the same route: choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. So does <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> for a new owner.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'tolls-and-tickets', 'chapter', 'owner-money', 'Toll notices and tickets arrive by mail and email. Read them into the system, check each line against the notice, and the matching, charges and emails follow.

## The work queue

**Money** > **Tolls and tickets**

1. Filter the queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged, Owner not billed, Staff, Charged not notified, Disputed.
2. Each toll shows its notice, kind, issuer, plate, when, amount and who it was matched to.
3. Add one by one with **Log one**, then **Save and match**. **Import a CSV** takes a statement file.

![](/guides/img/admin-19-tolls-desktop-baa198d0.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 500; address: carmacars.ca/admin/tolls; pins: 1 31.6 32.6, 2 59.7 52.0, 3 85.8 21.8")

## Inside a toll

1. Open a toll from the queue. Decide who pays: **Charge the renter**, **Bill to the owner** or **CarmaCars pays**.
2. Wrong notice? Press **Dispute**. Finance can also press **Match again**.
3. Reading profiles (top right on Read a notice) teach the reader an issuer''s layout. Paste a notice''s text under "Try it" to test one.

## Read a notice

1. Press **Read a notice**. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo (JPEG or PNG) or a CSV, under 15 MB.
2. Leave Reading profile on finding it from the text, or choose the issuer.
3. Press **Read it**. The file is stored first, then read in your browser.
4. Notices read lists every read with its status and counts.

![](/guides/img/admin-20-tolls-read-desktop-d733b5f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read; pins: 1 25.8 41.2, 2 36.1 52.2, 3 21.0 59.3, 4 25.8 79.7")

## Check the lines and import

1. The notice is on the left (**Zoom**, **Open the file**). The lines are on the right.
2. Check each line beside the notice: kind, issuer, notice number, plate, date and time, amount, fees, due date.
3. Fix what was read wrong, then press **Checked against the notice**. **Leave out** skips a line; **Put it back** returns it.
4. Press **Save as checked**, then **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/admin-21-tolls-review-desktop-c59d0a1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1150; address: carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read/76f10bea-9140-487b-89c8-a5cc8f15b59b; pins: 1 42.6 16.8, 2 56.7 43.8, 3 90.3 60.9, 4 76.0 38.0")

> Tip: Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and the administration fee, when "Charge renters matched with high confidence now" is ticked. Other lines go to the work queue or stay as exceptions with the reason.
', 'Tolls and tickets', 'The work queue, reading a notice, checking its lines and charging the right person.',
  'Toll notices and tickets arrive by mail and email. Read them into the system, check each line against the notice, and the matching, charges and emails follow.

## The work queue

**Money** > **Tolls and tickets**

1. Filter the queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged, Owner not billed, Staff, Charged not notified, Disputed.
2. Each toll shows its notice, kind, issuer, plate, when, amount and who it was matched to.
3. Add one by one with **Log one**, then **Save and match**. **Import a CSV** takes a statement file.

![](/guides/img/admin-19-tolls-desktop-baa198d0.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 500; address: carmacars.ca/admin/tolls; pins: 1 31.6 32.6, 2 59.7 52.0, 3 85.8 21.8")

## Inside a toll

1. Open a toll from the queue. Decide who pays: **Charge the renter**, **Bill to the owner** or **CarmaCars pays**.
2. Wrong notice? Press **Dispute**. Finance can also press **Match again**.
3. Reading profiles (top right on Read a notice) teach the reader an issuer''s layout. Paste a notice''s text under "Try it" to test one.

## Read a notice

1. Press **Read a notice**. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo (JPEG or PNG) or a CSV, under 15 MB.
2. Leave Reading profile on finding it from the text, or choose the issuer.
3. Press **Read it**. The file is stored first, then read in your browser.
4. Notices read lists every read with its status and counts.

![](/guides/img/admin-20-tolls-read-desktop-d733b5f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read; pins: 1 25.8 41.2, 2 36.1 52.2, 3 21.0 59.3, 4 25.8 79.7")

## Check the lines and import

1. The notice is on the left (**Zoom**, **Open the file**). The lines are on the right.
2. Check each line beside the notice: kind, issuer, notice number, plate, date and time, amount, fees, due date.
3. Fix what was read wrong, then press **Checked against the notice**. **Leave out** skips a line; **Put it back** returns it.
4. Press **Save as checked**, then **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/admin-21-tolls-review-desktop-c59d0a1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1150; address: carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read/76f10bea-9140-487b-89c8-a5cc8f15b59b; pins: 1 42.6 16.8, 2 56.7 43.8, 3 90.3 60.9, 4 76.0 38.0")

> Tip: Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and the administration fee, when "Charge renters matched with high confidence now" is ticked. Other lines go to the work queue or stay as exceptions with the reason.


## Deposit reviews before a release

Every returned booking with a deposit is reviewed twice before any of the deposit is released: Fleet signs fuel, kilometres, damage, late return, cleaning, tickets and highway tolls against the pickup photos, then Finance double-checks each, checks the toll operator and every ticket place. **Money** > **Payments** > **Deposit reviews** lists them; each booking has a **Deposit review** card. You may sign either side. To release a deposit before the review is done, use the settlement on the booking''s **Money** with the reason; it is recorded.

**Settings** > **Program settings**: **Deposit review required** (on), **Deposit review sweep days** (mon,wed,fri), **Deposit review toll url**, and **Deposit review ticket places**: each place''s name and official lookup link, edited as a list. A place you add applies to the reviews made after the change. **Money** > **Payments** > **Countdowns** shows the time left on every deposit hold, deposit return and plan payment, soonest first.

The accident card of a booking with the plan sold with the rental shows the renter''s own policy number and the provider''s claim page (Program settings, accident plan claim url). When the number was not captured at purchase, enter it on the booking''s accident card with **Enter the plan policy number**.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Toll notices and tickets arrive by mail and email. Read them into the system, check each line against the notice, and the matching, charges and emails follow.</p><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-the-work-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The work queue</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter the queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged, Owner not billed, Staff, Charged not notified, Disputed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each toll shows its notice, kind, issuer, plate, when, amount and who it was matched to.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add one by one with <b class="gd-ui">Log one</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and match</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Import a CSV</b> takes a statement file.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/tolls</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/500"><img src="/guides/img/admin-19-tolls-desktop-baa198d0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="500"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.6%;top:32.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:59.7%;top:52%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:85.8%;top:21.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-inside-a-toll" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Inside a toll</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open a toll from the queue. Decide who pays: <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Bill to the owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars pays</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Wrong notice? Press <b class="gd-ui">Dispute</b>. Finance can also press <b class="gd-ui">Match again</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Reading profiles (top right on Read a notice) teach the reader an issuer&#39;s layout. Paste a notice&#39;s text under &quot;Try it&quot; to test one.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-read-a-notice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read a notice</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read a notice</b>. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo (JPEG or PNG) or a CSV, under 15 MB.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave Reading profile on finding it from the text, or choose the issuer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. The file is stored first, then read in your browser.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Notices read lists every read with its status and counts.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-20-tolls-read-desktop-d733b5f1.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:41.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.1%;top:52.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:79.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-check-the-lines-and-import" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check the lines and import</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The notice is on the left (<b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Open the file</b>). The lines are on the right.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check each line beside the notice: kind, issuer, notice number, plate, date and time, amount, fees, due date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fix what was read wrong, then press <b class="gd-ui">Checked against the notice</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Leave out</b> skips a line; <b class="gd-ui">Put it back</b> returns it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as checked</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Confirm and import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read/76f10bea-9140-487b-89c8-a5cc8f15b59b</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1150"><img src="/guides/img/admin-21-tolls-review-desktop-c59d0a1c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1150"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.6%;top:16.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:56.7%;top:43.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:90.3%;top:60.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76%;top:38%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and the administration fee, when &quot;Charge renters matched with high confidence now&quot; is ticked. Other lines go to the work queue or stay as exceptions with the reason.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-deposit-reviews-before-a-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit reviews before a release</h2><p class="gd-p">Every returned booking with a deposit is reviewed twice before any of the deposit is released: Fleet signs fuel, kilometres, damage, late return, cleaning, tickets and highway tolls against the pickup photos, then Finance double-checks each, checks the toll operator and every ticket place. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payments</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Deposit reviews</b> lists them; each booking has a <b class="gd-ui">Deposit review</b> card. You may sign either side. To release a deposit before the review is done, use the settlement on the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> with the reason; it is recorded.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Deposit review required</b> (on), <b class="gd-ui">Deposit review sweep days</b> (mon,wed,fri), <b class="gd-ui">Deposit review toll url</b>, and <b class="gd-ui">Deposit review ticket places</b>: each place&#39;s name and official lookup link, edited as a list. A place you add applies to the reviews made after the change. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payments</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Countdowns</b> shows the time left on every deposit hold, deposit return and plan payment, soonest first.</p><p class="gd-p">The accident card of a booking with the plan sold with the rental shows the renter&#39;s own policy number and the provider&#39;s claim page (Program settings, accident plan claim url). When the number was not captured at purchase, enter it on the booking&#39;s accident card with <b class="gd-ui">Enter the plan policy number</b>.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'finance', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-requests', 'You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. **Money** opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: **To handle** (payments, deposits, refunds), **By day** (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), **All payments**, **Refunds**, **Deposits** and **Reconciliation**. **Owner money** lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.

## Your queue

Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.

![The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.](/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 20.3 24.3")

## Payments by day

**Money**, the **By day** tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.

1. Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.
3. At the end of the day count the drawer and press **Record the count**. The difference shows "balanced", or "over" or "short" with the amount.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.

## Payments, deposits, refunds

**Money**, the **To handle** tab.

1. Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank''s reason.
2. Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.
3. Refunds in progress. Press **Request the refund** and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then **Issue the refund**.
4. Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 865; address: carmacars.ca/va/money; pins: 1 10.6 60.3, 2 72.4 21.6, 3 73.2 33.8, 4 11.0 45.9")

## A payment received another way

An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.

1. Owner invoice: on **Payments, deposits, refunds**, find it under Owner invoices owing and press **Record payment**.
2. Renter: beside the failed payment, press **Paid another way**. Or open the booking''s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.
3. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.
4. Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press **Record payment**.

The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.

Each month''s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.

## Cards, holds and deposits given back

On the booking''s Money tab.

1. After the return, **Charge the renter**: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press **Charge $...**. Before the return, Rental charges, **A later charge**, with the same reason list on the renter''s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, **Charge the card on file as the deposit**.
2. A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or **Release**. **Hold expired**: nothing can be kept from it; press **Charge the card on file instead** (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.
3. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

## Settle a deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (**Keep the whole deposit (damage)**) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 7 days. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## Read a toll notice

1. Open **Tolls and tickets** and press **Read a notice**.
2. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.
3. Press **Read it**. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.
4. Press **Checked against the notice** on each line (**Leave out** to skip one), then **Save as checked** and **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read; pins: 2 19.5 44.1, 3 4.1 64.8, 4 4.1 89.7")

> Tip: In the work queue, **Match again** retries the match after a fix, and **Dispute** marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.

![The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice''s plate, date, amount and match.](/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls; pins: 1 23.6 12.2")

## Reconciliation and Turo trips

1. **Money**, the **Reconciliation** tab: press **Record a processor payout**, then **Match** it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.
2. **Turo trips**: press **Add a trip** for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press **Import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/turo; pins: 2 95.1 14.8")

## Deposits to release

A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: "Release the deposit for" the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.

1. Open the task: it opens the booking''s **Money** tab.
2. Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.
3. The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.

### Card payments outside the site and the card reader
On a booking''s **Money** tab: **Record card payment** records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). **Charge on reader** and **Hold deposit on reader** send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.

## Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)

Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**. A **The deposit hold expires soon** To do opens the booking: **Re-authorize the hold** places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or **Keep part (damage/fees)** for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, **Hold on the card on file**. Under **Money** > **Partner invoices** you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.

## Kickbacks and repairs

**Money** > **Kickbacks and repairs**: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under **Partner invoices** and press **Choose the car**. Add a repair cost with **Add a repair cost**; Fleet adds them on the car''s page too.

### A debit deposit''s card fee
A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable **Card processing fee for a debit deposit**, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.', 'Finance', 'Payments, deposits and refunds, tolls and tickets, reconciliation and Turo trips.',
