, each with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>, your variant&#39;s description and tracked link, and the photos in your order. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the photos (ZIP)</b>: 01 is your cover. <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the car&#39;s marketing set instead (its photos in other scenes, made on its listing).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post it on Facebook, open the new listing and copy its address. Back on <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> and paste the address. <b class="gd-ui">Let go</b> frees a claim you will not post.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Renewed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Updated</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b> when you do those on Facebook.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-words-to-use" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Words to use</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing a buyer reads says &quot;rent&quot;, &quot;rental&quot; or &quot;for rent&quot;. Every listing keeps the line &quot;Daily and weekly bookings only, not for sale&quot; and the price is for one day. The kit and the replies already follow this.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-the-auto-reply" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The auto-reply</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Auto-reply for this listing</b> has the steps and the text, with your listing&#39;s own link. While posting, scroll to <b class="gd-ui">Auto replies</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Meta AI replies</b>), turn it on, replace the draft with the text, then publish. It only answers the first &quot;Is this available?&quot;.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-the-inbox" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The inbox</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open facebook.com/marketplace/inbox, the Selling tab, oldest first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Use <b class="gd-ui">Inbox replies for this car</b> only: price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery, send your number. One message per reply, at most two to someone who does not answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Then <b class="gd-ui">Log an inbox session</b>: the chats, the replies and every number, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number is a lead credited to you, with a call-back task within 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-your-own-claude" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your own Claude</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Your Claude in Chrome</b> has the instructions to paste into Claude in your own Chrome, and the <b class="gd-ui">Academy lesson</b> that teaches them. Claude follows the same rules: the kit&#39;s words and the templates only, it stops at any Facebook security check or CAPTCHA and tells you, it never types a password, and it logs every post in your Marketing tab.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Stop and tell the Admin if Facebook removes a listing or restricts your account. Do not appeal and do not post it again.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'chapter', 'photo-shoots', 'Jobs go only to people on a shift. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Press **Claim this shift**. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the work planned so far. It updates as bookings come in.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.
', 'My shifts and My pay', 'Claim, give up and swap shifts, what you did on each, your hours, pay statements and pay details.',
  'Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example "On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans". Press **Claim this shift**: its jobs are yours on **Today** and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the shift''s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others'' show on **Today** under **Also on your shift**, and **Take it** takes one.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**. Each of you takes the other shift''s jobs.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.
